  "strategy": "# Approach and rationale\nThe central idea is to improve upon the parent solution by employing a multi-resolution optimization strategy that combines block-based initialization with gradient-based refinement. Unlike the parent's fixed block structure, our approach dynamically adjusts the number and size of active blocks, enabling better exploration of the solution space. We use a two-stage process: first, generating diverse initial guesses with variable block sizes, and second, refining these guesses with SLSQP optimization that enforces constraints explicitly. This addresses the limitation of the parent's homogeneous initializations and potential local optima trapping.\n\n# Mathematical specification\nWe define the step function h over n_points samples as:\n\n$$h(x) = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\chi_{[c_i, c_{i+1})}(x)$$\n\nwhere $a_i \\in [0, 1]$ are block heights, $c_i$ are sorted breakpoints, and $\\chi$ is the characteristic function. The constraints are:\n\n1. $\\sum_{i} a_i (c_{i+1} - c_i) = 1$\n2. $0 \\leq a_i \\leq 1$ for all i\n3. Breakpoints $0 \\leq c_1 < c_2 < \\dots < c_{m+1} \\leq 2$\n\n# Implementation procedure\n1. **Initialization**\n   - Start with a default resolution of n_points=256\n   - Generate 50 diverse initial guesses by randomly placing 2-10 blocks of variable lengths (2-64 points)\n   \n2. **Optimization**\n   - For each initial guess:\n     - Run SLSQP with:\n       - Objective: Max overlap after convolution\n       - Constraints: Integral constraint\n       - Bounds: [0, 1] for each point\n       - Description: Uses finite differences for gradient\n       \n3. **Post-processing**\n   - Select the best candidate based on overlap\n   - Refine with an additional SLSQP pass\n   - Ensure feasibility through projection\n   - Handle failures by reverting to the best initial guess\n\n# Search choices and useful variations\n- Initial blocks: Start with 2-10 blocks, sizes 2-64\n- Optimization settings: 1000 iterations per guess, ftol=1e-9\n- Refinement: 500 iterations for the best candidate\n\n# Compute budget and robustness\n- Time estimate: 1000s initial guesses + 500s refinement = 1500s worst case\n- Robustness: Built-in feasibility checks and fallbacks\n- Handling failures: Resume with backup candidates\n\n# Validation and return contract\n- Verify sum(h)=1 and h in [0,1]\n- Compute the objective using the evaluator\n- Ensure C5 is valid and improved",
